flowchart TB
  accTitle: Tiling an 8 by 20 times 20 by 8 product on a 4 by 4 array
  accDescr: The output C is four 4 by 4 tiles. Each output tile uses the matching four A rows and four B columns. For each tile, run once with k 0 through 15 and accumulate low, then run with k 16 through 19, k_len 4, and accumulate high. The first run clears the partial sum; the second adds to it.

  product["A: 8 × 20  ·  B: 20 × 8<br/>N = 4  ·  K_MAX = 16"]
  split["K chunks: 0–15 (k_len 16)  →  16–19 (k_len 4)<br/>A splits by row blocks; B splits by column blocks"]
  product --> split

  subgraph outputs["C: 8 × 8, four 4 × 4 output tiles"]
    direction TB
    subgraph row0["C rows 0–3"]
      direction LR
      c00["Tile (0,0)<br/>A rows 0–3 · B cols 0–3"]
      c01["Tile (0,1)<br/>A rows 0–3 · B cols 4–7"]
    end
    subgraph row1["C rows 4–7"]
      direction LR
      c10["Tile (1,0)<br/>A rows 4–7 · B cols 0–3"]
      c11["Tile (1,1)<br/>A rows 4–7 · B cols 4–7"]
    end
  end
  split --> outputs
  note["For each tile: run k 0–15 normally, then k 16–19 with accumulate high.<br/>The first run initializes C; the second keeps the partial sum.<br/>Load its A row block and B column block; read C when complete.<br/>Pad rows or columns beyond M or P with zero."]
  outputs -.-> note

  classDef tile fill:#dce9f7,stroke:#2c5d8f,color:#13263d
  classDef note fill:#f3f5f8,stroke:#60758b,color:#13263d
  class c00,c01,c10,c11 tile
  class note note
